# Undefined weak function references must link on DADAO (LLVM-085t / ISS-194).
#
# ELF gives an undefined weak symbol the value 0; the DADAO code image lives at
# 0xFC00_0000_0000, so the PC-relative displacement to 0 cannot be encoded and a
# veneer cannot bridge the 2^47 gap either.  lld now resolves such a reference
# to the place itself (RISC-V convention for relative-only ISAs) -- a self-loop
# -- and rewrites a `call` site to `jump` so that no RegRAS entry is pushed for
# a callee that can never pop it.  Strong/defined out-of-range symbols are
# unchanged (still a link-time error).
#
# 1) Undefined weak hook: links, the `&hook == 0` guard is taken (dead call),
#    guest exits 0, and the call site was rewritten to `jump [rb0, 0]`.
# RUN: %clang -target dadao-unknown-elf -nostdlib -Oz -c %e2e_dir/weak_undef_e2e.c -o %t.o
# RUN: %llvm_mc --triple=dadao-unknown-elf -filetype=obj %crt0 -o %t.crt0.o
# RUN: %ld -T %linker_script %t.crt0.o %t.o -o %t.elf
# RUN: timeout 30 %qemu -M dadao-m1 -kernel %t.elf -semihosting-config enable=on,target=native -display none -nographic -monitor none
# RUN: %llvm_objdump -d %t.elf | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WEAK

# 2) With a definition linked in, the same call is an ordinary in-range `call`
#    and the hook's value (9) reaches the caller: the special case applies only
#    to *undefined* weak symbols.
# RUN: %llvm_mc --triple=dadao-unknown-elf -filetype=obj %e2e_dir/weak_hook_def.s -o %t.def.o
# RUN: %ld -T %linker_script %t.crt0.o %t.o %t.def.o -o %t.def.elf
# RUN: %not timeout 30 %qemu -M dadao-m1 -kernel %t.def.elf -semihosting-config enable=on,target=native -display none -nographic -monitor none
# RUN: %llvm_objdump -d %t.def.elf | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DEF

# 3) Every PC-relative branch class to an undefined weak symbol becomes a
#    self-loop (displacement 0), REL26 included.
# RUN: %llvm_mc --triple=dadao-unknown-elf -filetype=obj %e2e_dir/weak_undef_forms.s -o %t.forms.o
# RUN: %ld -T %linker_script %t.forms.o -o %t.forms.elf
# RUN: %llvm_objdump -d %t.forms.elf | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FORMS

# 4) Strictness is not relaxed: a strong undefined symbol is still an error, and
#    a defined-but-far strong symbol is still an out-of-range error.
# RUN: %llvm_mc --triple=dadao-unknown-elf -filetype=obj %e2e_dir/weak_undef_strong.s -o %t.strong.o
# RUN: %not %ld -T %linker_script %t.strong.o -o %t.strong.elf 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STRONG
# RUN: %not %ld -T %linker_script --defsym=strong_fn=0xFC0010000000 %t.strong.o -o %t.far.elf 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAR

# WEAK: jump [rb0, 0]
# DEF: call [rb0,
# DEF-NOT: jump [rb0, 0]
# FORMS: jump [rb0, 0]
# FORMS: br.z {{.*}}[rb0, 0]
# FORMS: br.eq {{.*}}[rb0, 0]
# STRONG: undefined symbol: strong_fn
# FAR: relocation R_DADAO_REL26 out of range
# FAR: references 'strong_fn'
